{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/driver.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.star.driver\n     2\t  \"The dao.star Mode 1 driver (docs/design/dao.star.md, Flow and Liveness).\n     3\t\n     4\t   Per session the driver parks a real `yin.vm` continuation through\n     5\t   `dao.await`: one VM per session, whose program is pure sequential logic\n     6\t   reading its input medium (`in`) and emitting model values on its view medium\n     7\t   (`out`).  The driver does all the I/O.  It reads the session's routed\n     8\t   inputs with its own cursor, steps the parked continuation, drains the view\n     9\t   medium for the new model, mints the successor occurrence, appends the\n    10\t   consumption fact, and only after that append answers `ok` projects the\n    11\t   model to the egress medium.  The program never appends an effect.\n    12\t\n    13\t   Projection is the composition's pure `(project-fn occurrence-id model)`,\n    14\t   answering the complete SSE wire text; the root begin page is a separate\n    15\t   `(begin-fn lineage)`.  Subscribe and stale requests re-project the stored\n    16\t   latest `{:occurrence O :model m}` without resuming the VM.\n    17\t\n    18\t   The driver observes its grants before it consumes or projects, renews the\n    19\t   lineage lease on each consumed input and on its tick while a subscription is\n    20\t   open, stops at its bound (an input arriving then is handled as begin), and\n    21\t   releases on halt.\"\n    22\t  (:require [dao.await :as await]\n    23\t            [dao.star.facts :as facts]\n    24\t            [dao.star.lease :as lease]\n    25\t            [dao.star.signals :as signals]\n    26\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    27\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]))\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\t(defn- ok?\n    31\t  [r]\n    32\t  (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t(defn- new-ring\n    36\t  [capacity]\n    37\t  (let [r (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n    38\t                         ring/capacity-key capacity})]\n    39\t    (when-not (ok? r) (throw (ex-info \"cannot create a session medium\" {:outcome r})))\n    40\t    (:dao.stream/handle r)))\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\t(defn make-driver\n    44\t  \"Assemble the driver.  Config:\n    45\t     :facts :egress :begin     media handles (the session-facts writer, the\n    46\t                               egress writer, the begin handler's medium)\n    47\t     :tick                     the drivers' tick stream (handle)\n    48\t     :lineage-lease            the lineage-lease medium (handle, read for grants)\n    49\t     :exchange-lease           the exchange-lease medium (handle, read for grants)\n    50\t     :program                  a `dao.await` process reading `in`, writing `out`\n    51\t     :project-fn :begin-fn     the composition's projections\n    52\t     :units :lineage-renewal-interval :exchange-renewal-interval\n    53\t     :session-capacity         declared capacity of each session medium\n    54\t     :facts-capacity           declared capacity of the facts medium\"\n    55\t  [{:keys [program project-fn begin-fn] :as config}]\n    56\t  (when-not (and (map? program) (fn? project-fn) (fn? begin-fn))\n    57\t    (throw (ex-info \"the driver needs :program, :project-fn and :begin-fn\"\n    58\t                    {:refused :config})))\n    59\t  (atom {:config config\n    60\t         :begin-cursor (lease/oldest-cursor (:begin config))\n    61\t         :sessions {}}))\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\t(defn session-medium\n    65\t  \"The routed-input medium of lineage `s`, or nil: the router's forward target.\"\n    66\t  [driver s]\n    67\t  (get-in @driver [:sessions s :medium]))\n    68\t\n    69\t\n    70\t(defn sessions\n    71\t  [driver]\n    72\t  (set (keys (:sessions @driver))))\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\t(defn latest\n    76\t  \"The session's stored latest `{:occurrence O :model m}`, or nil.\"\n    77\t  [driver s]\n    78\t  (get-in @driver [:sessions s :latest]))\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\t(defn subscriptions\n    82\t  \"The exchange ids the session currently holds open as subscriptions.\"\n    83\t  [driver s]\n    84\t  (set (keys (get-in @driver [:sessions s :subs]))))\n    85\t\n    86\t\n    87\t(defn lineage-agent\n    88\t  [driver s]\n    89\t  (get-in @driver [:sessions s :agent]))\n    90\t\n    91\t\n    92\t(defn retire!\n    93\t  \"Retire the parked record of lineage `s`: the VM result and its media handles.\n    94\t   The reclaim procedure of the lineage lease; facts are never touched.\"\n    95\t  [driver s]\n    96\t  (swap! driver update :sessions dissoc s)\n    97\t  driver)\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   101\t;; Effects out\n   102\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   103\t\n   104\t(defn- emit!\n   105\t  [config effects]\n   106\t  (doseq [e effects]\n   107\t    (stream/append! (:egress config) e)))\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\t(defn- head\n   111\t  [x type]\n   112\t  {:http/exchange x :http/effect :http/head :http/status 200\n   113\t   :http/headers {\"content-type\" type \"cache-control\" \"no-cache\"}})\n   114\t\n   115\t\n   116\t(defn- chunk-fx\n   117\t  [x body]\n   118\t  {:http/exchange x :http/effect :http/chunk :http/body body})\n   119\t\n   120\t\n   121\t(defn- end\n   122\t  [x]\n   123\t  {:http/exchange x :http/effect :http/end})\n   124\t\n   125\t\n   126\t(defn- answer!\n   127\t  \"Head, one SSE projection, end: the reply to a one-shot exchange.\"\n   128\t  [config x occurrence model]\n   129\t  (emit! config [(head x \"text/event-stream\")\n   130\t                 (chunk-fx x ((:project-fn config) occurrence model))\n   131\t                 (end x)]))\n   132\t\n   133\t\n   134\t(defn- patch!\n   135\t  [config s]\n   136\t  (let [{:keys [occurrence model]} (:latest s)]\n   137\t    (doseq [x (keys (:subs s))]\n   138\t      (emit! config [(chunk-fx x ((:project-fn config) occurrence model))]))))\n   139\t\n   140\t\n   141\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   142\t;; Session construction\n   143\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   144\t\n   145\t(defn- decl\n   146\t  [capacity attribution]\n   147\t  (lease/medium-declaration capacity attribution))\n   148\t\n   149\t\n   150\t(defn- lineage-agent-config\n   151\t  [{:keys [tick lineage-lease facts units lineage-renewal-interval facts-capacity]} s]\n   152\t  (let [subject {:dao.star/lineage s}]\n   153\t    {:self subject :grantor lease/lineage-grantor :subject subject\n   154\t     :units units :renewal-interval lineage-renewal-interval\n   155\t     :resolver lease/resolver :resolver-bindings lease/resolver-bindings\n   156\t     :tick tick\n   157\t     :fact {:handle lineage-lease :source lease/lineage-lease-source\n   158\t            :medium (decl facts-capacity :per-author-media)}\n   159\t     :writer {:handle facts :medium (decl facts-capacity :envelope-key)}\n   160\t     :envelope {:dao.star/lineage s}}))\n   161\t\n   162\t\n   163\t(defn- exchange-agent-config\n   164\t  [{:keys [tick exchange-lease egress units exchange-renewal-interval facts-capacity]} x]\n   165\t  {:self :egress :grantor lease/exchange-grantor :subject {:http/exchange x}\n   166\t   :units units :renewal-interval exchange-renewal-interval\n   167\t   :resolver lease/resolver :resolver-bindings lease/resolver-bindings\n   168\t   :tick tick\n   169\t   :fact {:handle exchange-lease :source lease/exchange-lease-source\n   170\t          :medium (decl facts-capacity :per-author-media)}\n   171\t   :writer {:handle egress :medium (decl facts-capacity :per-author-media)}})\n   172\t\n   173\t\n   174\t(defn- last-model\n   175\t  \"Drain the view medium: the newest model emitted and the advanced cursor.\"\n   176\t  [handle cursor]\n   177\t  (let [r (lease/drain handle cursor)]\n   178\t    {:cursor (:cursor r) :model (last (:values r)) :emitted? (seq (:values r))}))\n   179\t\n   180\t\n   181\t(defn- begin!\n   182\t  \"Begin a lineage for exchange `x`: a fresh session with its own VM, the root\n   183\t   fact appended before anything is answered.  A root fact that is not accepted\n   184\t   starts nothing and answers nothing; the exchange lapses by silence.\"\n   185\t  [driver x]\n   186\t  (let [{:keys [program facts] :as config} (:config @driver)\n   187\t        s (str (random-uuid))\n   188\t        in (new-ring (:session-capacity config))\n   189\t        out (new-ring (:session-capacity config))\n   190\t        medium (new-ring (:session-capacity config))\n   191\t        result (await/run (update program :env merge {'in in 'out out}))\n   192\t        {:keys [cursor model]} (last-model out (lease/oldest-cursor out))]\n   193\t    (when (ok? (stream/append! facts (facts/root s)))\n   194\t      (swap! driver assoc-in [:sessions s]\n   195\t             {:lineage s :medium medium :cursor (lease/oldest-cursor medium)\n   196\t              :vm-in in :vm-out out :out-cursor cursor :result result\n   197\t              :latest {:occurrence s :model model} :subs {}\n   198\t              :agent (lease/make-agent (lineage-agent-config config s))})\n   199\t      (emit! config [(head x \"text/html\")\n   200\t                     (chunk-fx x ((:begin-fn config) s))\n   201\t                     (end x)]))))\n   202\t\n   203\t\n   204\t(defn begin-step!\n   205\t  \"Read the begin medium to `blocked`, beginning a lineage per message.\"\n   206\t  [driver]\n   207\t  (let [{:keys [config begin-cursor]} @driver\n   208\t        r (lease/drain (:begin config) begin-cursor)]\n   209\t    (swap! driver assoc :begin-cursor (:cursor r))\n   210\t    (doseq [m (:values r)\n   211\t            :when (and (map? m) (= :begin (:kind m)) (:exchange m))]\n   212\t      (begin! driver (:exchange m)))\n   213\t    driver))\n   214\t\n   215\t\n   216\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   217\t;; One session\n   218\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   219\t\n   220\t(defn- update-session!\n   221\t  [driver s f & args]\n   222\t  (swap! driver (fn [d] (if (contains? (:sessions d) s)\n   223\t                          (apply update-in d [:sessions s] f args)\n   224\t                          d))))\n   225\t\n   226\t\n   227\t(defn- publish!\n   228\t  \"Append the pending consumption fact; only when it answers `ok` does the new\n   229\t   occurrence become the latest and any UI carrying its id get projected.\"\n   230\t  [driver s]\n   231\t  (let [{:keys [config]} @driver\n   232\t        sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])\n   233\t        {:keys [successor predecessor model exchange halted?]} (:unpublished sess)]\n   234\t    (when (and sess (:unpublished sess))\n   235\t      (let [fact (if halted?\n   236\t                   (facts/ended s :halted)\n   237\t                   (facts/consumption s successor predecessor))]\n   238\t        (when (ok? (stream/append! (:facts config) fact))\n   239\t          (update-session! driver s\n   240\t                           (fn [x] (-> x\n   241\t                                       (dissoc :unpublished)\n   242\t                                       (cond-> (not halted?)\n   243\t                                         (assoc :latest {:occurrence successor :model model})))))\n   244\t          (let [sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])\n   245\t                occ (if halted? predecessor successor)]\n   246\t            (answer! config exchange occ model)\n   247\t            (when-not halted? (patch! config sess))\n   248\t            (if halted?\n   249\t              (lease/release! (:agent sess))\n   250\t              (lease/renew! (:agent sess)))))))))\n   251\t\n   252\t\n   253\t(defn- consume!\n   254\t  \"Step the parked continuation with one input and stage its successor.\"\n   255\t  [driver s m]\n   256\t  (let [sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])\n   257\t        input {:signals (signals/decode (:event m))}]\n   258\t    (stream/append! (:vm-in sess) input)\n   259\t    (let [result (await/resume (:result sess))\n   260\t          {:keys [cursor model emitted?]} (last-model (:vm-out sess) (:out-cursor sess))\n   261\t          halted? (not (:blocked? result))]\n   262\t      (update-session! driver s assoc :result result :out-cursor cursor)\n   263\t      (cond\n   264\t        (or emitted? halted?)\n   265\t        (do (update-session! driver s assoc :unpublished\n   266\t                             {:successor (str (random-uuid))\n   267\t                              :predecessor (get-in sess [:latest :occurrence])\n   268\t                              :model (if emitted? model (get-in sess [:latest :model]))\n   269\t                              :exchange (:exchange m)\n   270\t                              :halted? halted?})\n   271\t            (publish! driver s))\n   272\t\n   273\t        :else\n   274\t        (let [{:keys [occurrence model]} (:latest sess)]\n   275\t          (answer! (:config @driver) (:exchange m) occurrence model))))))\n   276\t\n   277\t\n   278\t(defn- subscribe!\n   279\t  [driver s m]\n   280\t  (let [{:keys [config]} @driver\n   281\t        x (:exchange m)\n   282\t        {:keys [occurrence model]} (get-in @driver [:sessions s :latest])]\n   283\t    (emit! config [(head x \"text/event-stream\")\n   284\t                   (chunk-fx x ((:project-fn config) occurrence model))])\n   285\t    (update-session! driver s assoc-in [:subs x]\n   286\t                     (lease/make-agent (exchange-agent-config config x)))))\n   287\t\n   288\t\n   289\t(defn- handle!\n   290\t  \"Handle one routed message.  Answers :wait when the message must stay unread\n   291\t   (no grant observed yet), :consumed otherwise.\"\n   292\t  [driver s m]\n   293\t  (let [{:keys [config]} @driver\n   294\t        sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])\n   295\t        agent (:agent sess)]\n   296\t    (cond\n   297\t      (= :terminal (:kind m))\n   298\t      (do (update-session! driver s update :subs dissoc (:exchange m)) :consumed)\n   299\t\n   300\t      (not (lease/granted? agent)) :wait\n   301\t\n   302\t      (lease/past-bound? agent)\n   303\t      (do (begin! driver (:exchange m)) :consumed)\n   304\t\n   305\t      (= :subscribe (:kind m)) (do (subscribe! driver s m) :consumed)\n   306\t\n   307\t      (and (= :input (:kind m))\n   308\t           (= (:token m) (get-in sess [:latest :occurrence])))\n   309\t      (do (consume! driver s m) :consumed)\n   310\t\n   311\t      :else\n   312\t      (let [{:keys [occurrence model]} (:latest sess)]\n   313\t        (answer! config (:exchange m) occurrence model)\n   314\t        :consumed))))\n   315\t\n   316\t\n   317\t(defn- read-messages!\n   318\t  [driver s]\n   319\t  (loop []\n   320\t    (let [sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])]\n   321\t      (when (and sess (not (:unpublished sess)))\n   322\t        (let [r (stream/next (:medium sess) (:cursor sess))]\n   323\t          (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   324\t            :dao.stream/ok\n   325\t            (when (= :consumed (handle! driver s (:dao.stream/value r)))\n   326\t              (update-session! driver s assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   327\t              (recur))\n   328\t\n   329\t            :dao.stream/gap\n   330\t            (do (update-session! driver s\n   331\t                                 (fn [x] (assoc x :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r) :subs {})))\n   332\t                (swap! (:agent sess) assoc :gapped? true)\n   333\t                (recur))\n   334\t\n   335\t            nil))))))\n   336\t\n   337\t\n   338\t(defn- tick-subscriptions!\n   339\t  \"On the tick: each subscription's holder observes its grant and any lapse,\n   340\t   and renews when due; a lapsed or gapped exchange is dropped.\"\n   341\t  [driver s]\n   342\t  (let [sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])]\n   343\t    (doseq [[x a] (:subs sess)]\n   344\t      (lease/step! a)\n   345\t      (if (or (:lapsed? @a) (:gapped? @a))\n   346\t        (update-session! driver s update :subs dissoc x)\n   347\t        (lease/renew-if-due! a)))\n   348\t    (when (seq (:subs (get-in @driver [:sessions s])))\n   349\t      (lease/renew-if-due! (:agent sess)))))\n   350\t\n   351\t\n   352\t(defn session-step!\n   353\t  [driver s]\n   354\t  (when-let [sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])]\n   355\t    (lease/step! (:agent sess))\n   356\t    (when (:unpublished sess) (publish! driver s))\n   357\t    (read-messages! driver s)\n   358\t    (tick-subscriptions! driver s))\n   359\t  driver)\n   360\t\n   361\t\n   362\t(defn driver-step!\n   363\t  \"One pass: begin handler, then every session.  Answers the driver.\"\n   364\t  [driver]\n   365\t  (begin-step! driver)\n   366\t  (doseq [s (sessions driver)]\n   367\t    (session-step! driver s))\n   368\t  driver)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/lease.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/router.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/facts.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/signals.cljc'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/lease.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/router.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/facts.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/signals.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.star.lease\n     2\t  \"The dao.lease compositions of dao.star Mode 1 (docs/design/dao.star.md,\n     3\t   Liveness): the stream-reading helper, the holder agent a driver threads per\n     4\t   lease, and the two grantor-side wrappers (exchange lease, lineage lease)\n     5\t   that author grants and drive the judge.\n     6\t\n     7\t   Nothing here reads a clock.  Time is the `:dao.lease/reading` data drained\n     8\t   from a tick stream the composition feeds, so every lapse is driven by\n     9\t   appending a tick.\"\n    10\t  (:require [dao.lease :as lease]\n    11\t            [dao.star.facts :as facts]\n    12\t            [dao.stream :as stream]))\n    13\t\n    14\t\n    15\t(defn- ok?\n    16\t  [r]\n    17\t  (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n    18\t\n    19\t\n    20\t(defn oldest-cursor\n    21\t  [handle]\n    22\t  (let [r (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-oldest)]\n    23\t    (when-not (ok? r)\n    24\t      (throw (ex-info \"cannot mint a cursor\" {:outcome r})))\n    25\t    (:dao.stream/cursor r)))\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\t(defn drain\n    29\t  \"Read `handle` from `cursor` to `blocked`, never waiting.  Answers\n    30\t   `{:cursor c :values [v...] :gap? bool :end? bool}`: a `gap` is noted and\n    31\t   reading continues from its recovery cursor, as the contract has it.\"\n    32\t  [handle cursor]\n    33\t  (loop [c cursor values [] gap? false]\n    34\t    (let [r (stream/next handle c)]\n    35\t      (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n    36\t        :dao.stream/ok (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj values (:dao.stream/value r)) gap?)\n    37\t        :dao.stream/gap (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) values true)\n    38\t        :dao.stream/end {:cursor c :values values :gap? gap? :end? true}\n    39\t        {:cursor c :values values :gap? gap? :end? false}))))\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    43\t;; Holder agent: one lease, held by a driver's control flow\n    44\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    45\t\n    46\t(defn make-agent\n    47\t  \"A holder over `lease/make-holder` plus the cursors its control flow drains.\n    48\t   `config` is `make-holder`'s, less the cursors (minted here at the oldest\n    49\t   anchor, so a grant already on the medium is observed).  `:envelope` is merged\n    50\t   into every fact the agent appends (the lineage lease stamps\n    51\t   `:dao.star/lineage` here, which is what the judge's resolver attributes by).\n    52\t   Answers an atom holding the agent state.\"\n    53\t  [{:keys [tick fact writer envelope] :as config}]\n    54\t  (let [wired (lease/make-holder\n    55\t                (assoc config\n    56\t                       :tick {:handle tick :cursor (oldest-cursor tick)}\n    57\t                       :fact {:handle (:handle fact)\n    58\t                              :cursor (oldest-cursor (:handle fact))\n    59\t                              :source (:source fact)\n    60\t                              :medium (:medium fact)}\n    61\t                       :writer writer))]\n    62\t    (atom {:holder (:holder wired)\n    63\t           :tick (:tick wired)\n    64\t           :fact (:fact wired)\n    65\t           :writer (:writer wired)\n    66\t           :envelope (or envelope {})\n    67\t           :reading nil\n    68\t           :lapsed? false\n    69\t           :gapped? false\n    70\t           :release nil})))\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\t(defn- lease-id\n    74\t  [a]\n    75\t  (get-in a [:holder :grant :dao.lease/lease]))\n    76\t\n    77\t\n    78\t(defn step!\n    79\t  \"One control-flow pass of the holder: drain its own tick cursor for the\n    80\t   newest reading, drain the fact cursor observing its grant (before anything\n    81\t   else) and any `:lapsed` record for its lease.  A `gap` on either cursor\n    82\t   marks the agent `:gapped?`: it renews nothing from then on.  Answers the\n    83\t   new state.\"\n    84\t  [agent]\n    85\t  (swap!\n    86\t    agent\n    87\t    (fn [a]\n    88\t      (let [t (drain (get-in a [:tick :handle]) (get-in a [:tick :cursor]))\n    89\t            reading (or (some-> (filter #(= :dao.lease/tick (:dao.lease/event %))\n    90\t                                        (:values t))\n    91\t                                last\n    92\t                                :dao.lease/reading)\n    93\t                        (:reading a))\n    94\t            f (drain (get-in a [:fact :handle]) (get-in a [:fact :cursor]))\n    95\t            a (-> a\n    96\t                  (assoc :reading reading)\n    97\t                  (assoc-in [:tick :cursor] (:cursor t))\n    98\t                  (assoc-in [:fact :cursor] (:cursor f))\n    99\t                  (update :gapped? #(or % (:gap? f))))]\n   100\t        (reduce\n   101\t          (fn [a v]\n   102\t            (cond\n   103\t              (and (nil? (get-in a [:holder :grant])) reading)\n   104\t              (update a :holder lease/observe-grant (get-in a [:fact :source]) v reading)\n   105\t\n   106\t              (and (= :dao.lease/lapsed (:dao.lease/status v))\n   107\t                   (some? (lease-id a))\n   108\t                   (= (lease-id a) (:dao.lease/lease v)))\n   109\t              (assoc a :lapsed? true)\n   110\t\n   111\t              :else a))\n   112\t          a\n   113\t          (:values f))))))\n   114\t\n   115\t\n   116\t(defn holding?\n   117\t  \"May the control flow act: a grant observed, not stopped, not at its bound,\n   118\t   not lapsed, and no gap seen.\"\n   119\t  [agent]\n   120\t  (let [a @agent]\n   121\t    (boolean (and (not (:lapsed? a))\n   122\t                  (not (:gapped? a))\n   123\t                  (some? (:reading a))\n   124\t                  (lease/holding? (:holder a) (:reading a))))))\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t(defn granted?\n   128\t  [agent]\n   129\t  (some? (get-in @agent [:holder :grant])))\n   130\t\n   131\t\n   132\t(defn past-bound?\n   133\t  \"True once the agent has left the lease for good: it lapsed, was released,\n   134\t   or reached its bound.  A gap is not that: the agent renews nothing after one\n   135\t   but the lease is not known to be over.\"\n   136\t  [agent]\n   137\t  (let [a @agent]\n   138\t    (boolean (or (:lapsed? a)\n   139\t                 (get-in a [:holder :released?])\n   140\t                 (get-in a [:holder :bound-reached?])\n   141\t                 (and (some? (:reading a)) (some? (get-in a [:holder :grant]))\n   142\t                      (lease/at-bound? (:holder a) (:reading a)))))))\n   143\t\n   144\t\n   145\t(defn- append-renewal!\n   146\t  [agent]\n   147\t  (let [a @agent\n   148\t        fact (merge (lease/renewal (lease-id a)) (:envelope a))\n   149\t        outcome (stream/append! (get-in a [:writer :handle]) fact)]\n   150\t    (swap! agent update :holder lease/observe-renewal (:reading a) outcome)\n   151\t    outcome))\n   152\t\n   153\t\n   154\t(defn renew-if-due!\n   155\t  \"Renew when the holder's interval has been reached.  Answers true when a\n   156\t   renewal was appended.\"\n   157\t  [agent]\n   158\t  (let [a @agent]\n   159\t    (boolean\n   160\t      (when (and (holding? agent) (lease/due-to-renew? (:holder a) (:reading a)))\n   161\t        (append-renewal! agent)\n   162\t        true))))\n   163\t\n   164\t\n   165\t(defn renew!\n   166\t  \"Renew now, on a consumed input.  A holder that is not holding renews\n   167\t   nothing.\"\n   168\t  [agent]\n   169\t  (boolean (when (holding? agent) (append-renewal! agent) true)))\n   170\t\n   171\t\n   172\t(defn release!\n   173\t  \"Release on halt.  The release fact is kept until its append answers ok, so a\n   174\t   failed append retries the same fact.\"\n   175\t  [agent]\n   176\t  (let [a @agent]\n   177\t    (when (and (granted? agent) (not (get-in a [:holder :released?])))\n   178\t      (let [{:keys [holder release]} (lease/stop (:holder a))]\n   179\t        (swap! agent assoc :holder holder :release (merge release (:envelope a)))))\n   180\t    (when-let [fact (:release @agent)]\n   181\t      (when (ok? (stream/append! (get-in @agent [:writer :handle]) fact))\n   182\t        (swap! agent assoc :release nil :released-sent? true)))\n   183\t    agent))\n   184\t\n   185\t\n   186\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   187\t;; Grantor side: exchange lease\n   188\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   189\t\n   190\t(def resolver-bindings #{:per-author-media :envelope-key})\n   191\t\n   192\t(def exchange-source :egress)\n   193\t(def lineage-source :session-facts)\n   194\t(def exchange-lease-source :exchange-lease)\n   195\t(def lineage-lease-source :lineage-lease)\n   196\t(def exchange-grantor :boundary-judge)\n   197\t(def lineage-grantor :lineage-judge)\n   198\t\n   199\t\n   200\t(defn resolver\n   201\t  \"The one attribution the star compositions share.  Per-author media: the\n   202\t   source names the author.  Envelope key: the session-facts medium is written\n   203\t   only by session drivers, each stamping `:dao.star/lineage`, and that stamp\n   204\t   names the author.  A fact's own claim of authorship is never consulted.\"\n   205\t  [source fact]\n   206\t  (if (= lineage-source source)\n   207\t    (when-let [s (:dao.star/lineage fact)] {:dao.star/lineage s})\n   208\t    (case source\n   209\t      :egress :egress\n   210\t      :exchange-lease exchange-grantor\n   211\t      :lineage-lease lineage-grantor\n   212\t      nil)))\n   213\t\n   214\t\n   215\t(defn medium-declaration\n   216\t  [capacity attribution]\n   217\t  {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity capacity\n   218\t   :value-domain :portable-values :attribution attribution})\n   219\t\n   220\t\n   221\t(defn make-exchange-lease\n   222\t  \"The grantor half of the exchange lease, composed inside the peer holding the\n   223\t   HTTP boundary.  Config:\n   224\t     :ingress :egress :lease-medium  the three media (handles)\n   225\t     :tick                           the judge's tick stream (handle)\n   226\t     :open-exchanges :close-exchange the boundary's inventory and reclaim\n   227\t     :units :duration :cadence :tolerance\n   228\t     :capacity                       declared capacity of the egress medium\n   229\t   The judge reads the egress medium for the responders' renewals and writes\n   230\t   grants and `:lapsed` to the lease medium.  Policy ends the lease of an\n   231\t   exchange the inventory no longer holds (peer close, gap reconciliation), and\n   232\t   reclaim is the boundary's idempotent `close-exchange`, reporting success when\n   233\t   the exchange is not open afterwards.\"\n   234\t  [{:keys [ingress egress lease-medium tick open-exchanges close-exchange\n   235\t           units duration cadence tolerance capacity]}]\n   236\t  (let [reclaim (fn [subject]\n   237\t                  (let [id (:http/exchange subject)]\n   238\t                    (close-exchange id)\n   239\t                    (not (contains? (open-exchanges) id))))\n   240\t        policy (fn [entry _now]\n   241\t                 (not (contains? (open-exchanges)\n   242\t                                 (:http/exchange (:subject entry)))))\n   243\t        made (lease/make-judge\n   244\t               {:units units :cadence cadence :tolerance tolerance\n   245\t                :resolver resolver :resolver-bindings resolver-bindings\n   246\t                :reclaim reclaim :policy policy\n   247\t                :writer lease-medium :self exchange-grantor\n   248\t                :ticks [{:handle tick :cursor (oldest-cursor tick)}]\n   249\t                :media [{:handle egress :cursor (oldest-cursor egress)\n   250\t                         :source exchange-source\n   251\t                         :medium (medium-declaration capacity :per-author-media)}]})]\n   252\t    (atom {:judge (:judge made) :step (:step made)\n   253\t           :ingress ingress :ingress-cursor (oldest-cursor ingress)\n   254\t           :open-exchanges open-exchanges\n   255\t           :duration duration :leased #{}})))\n   256\t\n   257\t\n   258\t(defn- grant-exchange\n   259\t  [x id]\n   260\t  (swap! x (fn [s]\n   261\t             (-> s\n   262\t                 (update :judge lease/author-grant\n   263\t                         (lease/grant (lease/mint-lease-id) {:http/exchange id}\n   264\t                                      :egress (:duration s)))\n   265\t                 (update :leased conj id))))\n   266\t  x)\n   267\t\n   268\t\n   269\t(defn exchange-lease-step!\n   270\t  \"One pass: observe the ingress for each `:http/request` and grant its\n   271\t   exchange unsolicited; on an ingress gap reconcile against the inventory (an\n   272\t   open exchange without a lease is granted afresh; a leased exchange absent\n   273\t   from the inventory is ended by the judge's policy with cause `:policy`);\n   274\t   then one judge pass.  Answers the atom.\"\n   275\t  [x]\n   276\t  (let [s @x\n   277\t        r (drain (:ingress s) (:ingress-cursor s))\n   278\t        open ((:open-exchanges s))]\n   279\t    (swap! x assoc :ingress-cursor (:cursor r))\n   280\t    (doseq [v (:values r)\n   281\t            :when (= :http/request (:http/event v))\n   282\t            :let [id (:http/exchange v)]\n   283\t            :when (and (contains? open id) (not (contains? (:leased @x) id)))]\n   284\t      (grant-exchange x id))\n   285\t    (when (:gap? r)\n   286\t      (doseq [id open :when (not (contains? (:leased @x) id))]\n   287\t        (grant-exchange x id)))\n   288\t    ;; Forget what is closed: its lease is the judge's to end.\n   289\t    (swap! x update :leased #(into #{} (filter open) %))\n   290\t    (swap! x (fn [s] (update s :judge (:step s))))\n   291\t    x))\n   292\t\n   293\t\n   294\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   295\t;; Grantor side: lineage lease\n   296\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   297\t\n   298\t(defn make-lineage-lease\n   299\t  \"The grantor half of the lineage lease.  Config:\n   300\t     :facts          the session-facts medium (handle)\n   301\t     :lease-medium   where grants and `:lapsed` are written (handle)\n   302\t     :tick           the judge's tick stream (handle)\n   303\t     :retire!        (fn [lineage]) retiring the parked record\n   304\t     :units :duration :max :cadence :tolerance :capacity\n   305\t   Each root fact read grants unsolicited, subject and holder\n   306\t   `{:dao.star/lineage S}`.  The judge reads the same medium for the drivers'\n   307\t   renewals and releases, attributed by the `:dao.star/lineage` envelope key.\"\n   308\t  [{:keys [lease-medium tick retire! units duration cadence tolerance capacity]\n   309\t    cap :max session-facts :facts}]\n   310\t  (let [made (lease/make-judge\n   311\t               {:units units :cadence cadence :tolerance tolerance\n   312\t                :resolver resolver :resolver-bindings resolver-bindings\n   313\t                :reclaim (fn [subject]\n   314\t                           (retire! (:dao.star/lineage subject))\n   315\t                           true)\n   316\t                :writer lease-medium :self lineage-grantor\n   317\t                :ticks [{:handle tick :cursor (oldest-cursor tick)}]\n   318\t                :media [{:handle session-facts :cursor (oldest-cursor session-facts)\n   319\t                         :source lineage-source\n   320\t                         :medium (medium-declaration capacity :envelope-key)}]})]\n   321\t    (atom {:judge (:judge made) :step (:step made)\n   322\t           :facts session-facts :facts-cursor (oldest-cursor session-facts)\n   323\t           :duration duration :max cap})))\n   324\t\n   325\t\n   326\t(defn lineage-lease-step!\n   327\t  \"One pass: grant each newly read root, then one judge pass.\"\n   328\t  [x]\n   329\t  (let [s @x\n   330\t        r (drain (:facts s) (:facts-cursor s))]\n   331\t    (swap! x assoc :facts-cursor (:cursor r))\n   332\t    (doseq [v (:values r)\n   333\t            :when (and (map? v) (= :root (facts/fact-kind v)))\n   334\t            :let [subject {:dao.star/lineage (:dao.star/lineage v)}]]\n   335\t      (swap! x update :judge lease/author-grant\n   336\t             (lease/grant (lease/mint-lease-id) subject subject (:duration s)\n   337\t                          (when (:max s) {:dao.lease/max (:max s)}))))\n   338\t    (swap! x (fn [s] (update s :judge (:step s))))\n   339\t    x))\n     1\t(ns dao.star.router\n     2\t  \"The dao.star Mode 1 router (docs/design/dao.star.md, Routing and Sessions\n     3\t   and request kinds).\n     4\t\n     5\t   A stepped interpreter: each pass reads the ingress with its own cursor to\n     6\t   `blocked`, then drains the session-facts and lineage-lease cursors to\n     7\t   `blocked` folding them into the index, and only then classifies what the\n     8\t   ingress gave it.  Unknown is judged after both drains, never before, which\n     9\t   is what makes a just-published token impossible to answer as begin.\n    10\t\n    11\t   The router holds no token table of its own: the index is derived from the\n    12\t   two media it reads, and it forwards a request to the medium of the session\n    13\t   its token names, with every later terminal event of that exchange.  The\n    14\t   boundary never routes, and a gap forwards nothing.\"\n    15\t  (:require [dao.star.facts :as facts]\n    16\t            [dao.star.lease :as lease]\n    17\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    18\t            #?(:clj [dao.stream.remote]))\n    19\t  #?(:clj (:import [dao.stream.remote ReflectionHandle])))\n    20\t\n    21\t\n    22\t(defn- reflection?\n    23\t  [handle]\n    24\t  #?(:clj (instance? ReflectionHandle handle)\n    25\t     :default (and false handle)))\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\t(defn classify\n    29\t  \"Pure: the kind of request `(method, path)` under `index`.\n    30\t     {:kind :begin}                         `/`, or a token of an ended or\n    31\t                                            unknown lineage\n    32\t     {:kind :subscribe :lineage S}          `/s/<token>`, token live\n    33\t     {:kind :input :lineage S :token t}     `/k/<token>`, token current\n    34\t     {:kind :stale :lineage S :token t}     `/k/<token>`, token consumed\n    35\t     {:kind :unrouted}                      any other path\"\n    36\t  [index path]\n    37\t  (let [[_ head token] (re-matches #\"/(s|k)/([^/]+)\" (str path))\n    38\t        tok (when head (facts/resolve-token index token))]\n    39\t    (cond\n    40\t      (= \"/\" path) {:kind :begin}\n    41\t      (nil? head) {:kind :unrouted}\n    42\t      (contains? #{:ended :unknown} (:kind tok)) {:kind :begin}\n    43\t      (= \"s\" head) {:kind :subscribe :lineage (:lineage tok) :token token}\n    44\t      (= :current (:kind tok)) {:kind :input :lineage (:lineage tok) :token token}\n    45\t      :else {:kind :stale :lineage (:lineage tok) :token token})))\n    46\t\n    47\t\n    48\t(defn make-router\n    49\t  \"Assemble the router.  Config:\n    50\t     :ingress        the boundary's ingress medium (may be a reflection)\n    51\t     :facts          the session-facts medium, a direct handle\n    52\t     :lease          the lineage-lease medium, a direct handle\n    53\t     :begin          the begin handler's medium (handle)\n    54\t     :session-medium (fn [lineage] -> handle or nil)\n    55\t   The facts and lease handles are classification media: a reflection answers\n    56\t   `blocked` while its request is pending, which says nothing about the source,\n    57\t   so the router refuses at assembly (ex-info `:refused :co-located`) unless\n    58\t   both are direct handles declared `:co-located? true`.\"\n    59\t  [{:keys [ingress facts lease begin session-medium co-located?] :as config}]\n    60\t  (when-not (and co-located?\n    61\t                 (not (reflection? facts))\n    62\t                 (not (reflection? lease)))\n    63\t    (throw (ex-info \"the router reads its classification media directly: declare :co-located? true with direct (non-reflection) handles\"\n    64\t                    {:refused :co-located})))\n    65\t  (when-not (and ingress facts lease begin (fn? session-medium))\n    66\t    (throw (ex-info \"the router needs :ingress :facts :lease :begin :session-medium\"\n    67\t                    {:refused :config :config (dissoc config :ingress :facts :lease :begin)})))\n    68\t  (atom {:config config\n    69\t         :ingress-cursor (lease/oldest-cursor ingress)\n    70\t         :facts-cursor (lease/oldest-cursor facts)\n    71\t         :lease-cursor (lease/oldest-cursor lease)\n    72\t         :index facts/empty-index\n    73\t         :routes {}\n    74\t         :gaps 0}))\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\t(defn index\n    78\t  [router]\n    79\t  (:index @router))\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\t(defn- forward!\n    83\t  \"Append `message` to `handle`; a non-ok answer is loss, dropped silently.\"\n    84\t  [handle message]\n    85\t  (when handle\n    86\t    (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! handle message)))))\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t(defn- route!\n    90\t  [router event]\n    91\t  (let [{:keys [config index]} @router\n    92\t        x (:http/exchange event)]\n    93\t    (case (:http/event event)\n    94\t      :http/request\n    95\t      (let [c (classify index (:http/path event))\n    96\t            target (case (:kind c)\n    97\t                     :begin (:begin config)\n    98\t                     :unrouted nil\n    99\t                     ((:session-medium config) (:lineage c)))]\n   100\t        (when (and target\n   101\t                   (forward! target {:exchange x :kind (:kind c) :token (:token c)\n   102\t                                     :lineage (:lineage c) :event event}))\n   103\t          (swap! router assoc-in [:routes x] target)))\n   104\t\n   105\t      (:http/ended :http/closed)\n   106\t      (when-let [target (get-in @router [:routes x])]\n   107\t        (swap! router update :routes dissoc x)\n   108\t        (forward! target {:exchange x :kind :terminal :event event}))\n   109\t\n   110\t      nil)))\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\t(defn router-step!\n   114\t  \"One pass, in the spec's order.  Answers the router.\"\n   115\t  [router]\n   116\t  (let [s @router\n   117\t        {:keys [ingress facts lease]} (:config s)\n   118\t        in (lease/drain ingress (:ingress-cursor s))\n   119\t        fs (lease/drain facts (:facts-cursor s))\n   120\t        ls (lease/drain lease (:lease-cursor s))]\n   121\t    (swap! router\n   122\t           (fn [s]\n   123\t             (-> s\n   124\t                 (assoc :ingress-cursor (:cursor in)\n   125\t                        :facts-cursor (:cursor fs)\n   126\t                        :lease-cursor (:cursor ls))\n   127\t                 (update :gaps + (if (:gap? in) 1 0))\n   128\t                 (update :index #(reduce facts/index-step % (:values fs)))\n   129\t                 (update :index #(reduce facts/index-step % (:values ls))))))\n   130\t    (doseq [event (:values in)\n   131\t            :when (map? event)]\n   132\t      (route! router event))\n   133\t    router))\n     1\t(ns dao.star.facts\n     2\t  \"The session-facts grammar of dao.star Mode 1 (docs/design/dao.star.md,\n     3\t   Sessions and request kinds), as pure functions.\n     4\t\n     5\t   Three facts are written, only through the constructors here: a lineage's\n     6\t   root, a consumption (one transition of one lineage), and the end of a\n     7\t   lineage.  `valid-fact?` guards readers: anything else on the medium (lease\n     8\t   renewals, foreign values) is noise to be ignored, never thrown on.\n     9\t\n    10\t   `index-step` folds one fact, or one lineage-lease record, into the\n    11\t   occurrence -> lineage -> current index a router materializes.  The index is\n    12\t   derived state, rebuilt from the media; nothing here keeps a table.\")\n    13\t\n    14\t\n    15\t(defn root\n    16\t  \"A lineage's first fact: its id is its root occurrence's id.\"\n    17\t  [lineage]\n    18\t  {:dao.star/lineage lineage :dao.star/occurrence lineage})\n    19\t\n    20\t\n    21\t(defn consumption\n    22\t  \"One transition: `successor` replaces `predecessor` as the lineage's\n    23\t   current occurrence.\"\n    24\t  [lineage successor predecessor]\n    25\t  {:dao.star/lineage lineage\n    26\t   :dao.star/occurrence successor\n    27\t   :dao.star/predecessor predecessor})\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\t(defn ended\n    31\t  \"The lineage's program finished (`reason`, a keyword such as :halted).\"\n    32\t  [lineage reason]\n    33\t  {:dao.star/lineage lineage :dao.star/ended reason})\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\t(defn- id?\n    37\t  [x]\n    38\t  (and (string? x) (not (empty? x))))\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\t(defn fact-kind\n    42\t  \"`:root`, `:consumption`, `:ended`, or nil for anything else.  Facts have\n    43\t   exactly the keys the constructors produce; a value with more is not one.\"\n    44\t  [x]\n    45\t  (when (map? x)\n    46\t    (let [ks (set (keys x))\n    47\t          lineage (:dao.star/lineage x)\n    48\t          occurrence (:dao.star/occurrence x)]\n    49\t      (cond\n    50\t        (not (id? lineage)) nil\n    51\t\n    52\t        (and (= ks #{:dao.star/lineage :dao.star/occurrence})\n    53\t             (= lineage occurrence))\n    54\t        :root\n    55\t\n    56\t        (and (= ks #{:dao.star/lineage :dao.star/occurrence :dao.star/predecessor})\n    57\t             (id? occurrence)\n    58\t             (id? (:dao.star/predecessor x))\n    59\t             (not= occurrence (:dao.star/predecessor x)))\n    60\t        :consumption\n    61\t\n    62\t        (and (= ks #{:dao.star/lineage :dao.star/ended})\n    63\t             (keyword? (:dao.star/ended x)))\n    64\t        :ended\n    65\t\n    66\t        :else nil))))\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\t(defn valid-fact?\n    70\t  [x]\n    71\t  (some? (fact-kind x)))\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t(def empty-index\n    75\t  {:occurrence {}    ; occurrence -> lineage\n    76\t   :current {}       ; lineage -> its current occurrence\n    77\t   :ended #{}        ; lineages that are over (halted or lapsed)\n    78\t   :leases {}})      ; lease id -> lineage, from lineage-lease grants\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\t(defn- lineage-subject\n    82\t  [fact]\n    83\t  (let [s (:dao.lease/subject fact)]\n    84\t    (when (and (map? s) (id? (:dao.star/lineage s)))\n    85\t      (:dao.star/lineage s))))\n    86\t\n    87\t\n    88\t(defn index-step\n    89\t  \"Fold one read value into the index.  A valid session fact advances it; a\n    90\t   lineage-lease `:accepted` records which lineage a lease is for and a\n    91\t   `:lapsed` ends that lineage for routing; anything else, and any fact that\n    92\t   does not follow from the index (a consumption whose predecessor is not\n    93\t   current), changes nothing.\"\n    94\t  [index x]\n    95\t  (case (fact-kind x)\n    96\t    :root (let [s (:dao.star/lineage x)]\n    97\t            (if (contains? (:current index) s)\n    98\t              index\n    99\t              (-> index\n   100\t                  (assoc-in [:current s] s)\n   101\t                  (assoc-in [:occurrence s] s))))\n   102\t\n   103\t    :consumption (let [s (:dao.star/lineage x)\n   104\t                       o2 (:dao.star/occurrence x)]\n   105\t                   (if (and (= (:dao.star/predecessor x) (get-in index [:current s]))\n   106\t                            (not (contains? (:occurrence index) o2)))\n   107\t                     (-> index\n   108\t                         (assoc-in [:current s] o2)\n   109\t                         (assoc-in [:occurrence o2] s))\n   110\t                     index))\n   111\t\n   112\t    :ended (update index :ended conj (:dao.star/lineage x))\n   113\t\n   114\t    (cond\n   115\t      (and (map? x)\n   116\t           (= :dao.lease/accepted (:dao.lease/status x))\n   117\t           (lineage-subject x)\n   118\t           (some? (:dao.lease/lease x)))\n   119\t      (assoc-in index [:leases (:dao.lease/lease x)] (lineage-subject x))\n   120\t\n   121\t      (and (map? x)\n   122\t           (= :dao.lease/lapsed (:dao.lease/status x)))\n   123\t      (if-let [s (get-in index [:leases (:dao.lease/lease x)])]\n   124\t        (update index :ended conj s)\n   125\t        index)\n   126\t\n   127\t      :else index)))\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(defn resolve-token\n   131\t  \"What a token names under `index`:\n   132\t     {:kind :current :lineage S}   the lineage's current occurrence\n   133\t     {:kind :consumed :lineage S}  an occurrence that has a successor\n   134\t     {:kind :ended :lineage S}     a token of a halted or lapsed lineage\n   135\t     {:kind :unknown}              never seen\"\n   136\t  [index token]\n   137\t  (if-let [s (get-in index [:occurrence token])]\n   138\t    (cond\n   139\t      (contains? (:ended index) s) {:kind :ended :lineage s}\n   140\t      (= token (get-in index [:current s])) {:kind :current :lineage s}\n   141\t      :else {:kind :consumed :lineage s})\n   142\t    {:kind :unknown}))\n     1\t(ns dao.star.signals\n     2\t  \"Decode a request's client signals from an `:http/request` event\n     3\t   (docs/design/dao.star.md, Signals).\n     4\t\n     5\t   Signals are the client's unverified claim, so `decode` is total: a missing,\n     6\t   malformed or non-map input answers `{}` and nothing throws.  GET and DELETE\n     7\t   carry them in the query parameter the spec names, every other method in the\n     8\t   JSON body.  The JSON parse is the host's; a host without one decodes\n     9\t   nothing.\"\n    10\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n    11\t            [dao.host.bytes :as bytes]\n    12\t            [dao.host.text :as text]\n    13\t            #?(:clj [clojure.data.json :as json])))\n    14\t\n    15\t\n    16\t(defn- parse-json\n    17\t  [s]\n    18\t  #?(:cljd nil\n    19\t     :clj (json/read-str s :key-fn keyword)\n    20\t     :cljs (js->clj (js/JSON.parse s) :keywordize-keys true)))\n    21\t\n    22\t\n    23\t(defn- url-decode\n    24\t  [s]\n    25\t  #?(:cljd nil\n    26\t     :clj (java.net.URLDecoder/decode ^String s \"UTF-8\")\n    27\t     :cljs (js/decodeURIComponent (str/replace s \"+\" \" \"))))\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\t(defn- body-text\n    31\t  [body]\n    32\t  (cond (string? body) body\n    33\t        (bytes/bytes? body) (text/utf8-decode body)\n    34\t        :else nil))\n    35\t\n    36\t\n    37\t(defn- query-param\n    38\t  [query k]\n    39\t  (when (string? query)\n    40\t    (some (fn [pair]\n    41\t            (let [[name value] (str/split pair #\"=\" 2)]\n    42\t              (when (= k name) (or value \"\"))))\n    43\t          (str/split query #\"&\"))))\n    44\t\n    45\t\n    46\t(defn decode\n    47\t  \"The signals map of request `event`, or `{}`.\"\n    48\t  [event]\n    49\t  (try\n    50\t    (let [raw (if (contains? #{:get :delete} (:http/method event))\n    51\t                (some-> (query-param (:http/query event) \"datastar\") url-decode)\n    52\t                (body-text (:http/body event)))\n    53\t          parsed (when (and (string? raw) (not (empty? raw))) (parse-json raw))]\n    54\t      (if (map? parsed) parsed {}))\n    55\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ {})))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The router follows the required ingress-first drain order. I’ve found potential gaps in holder discipline and input consumption: the initial HTML response precedes grant observation, and an input that emits no model appears to leave its token current. I’m tracing those paths and the subscription renewal behavior against the tests."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '46,255p' src/cljc/dao/star/lease.cljc; sed -n '78,103p' docs/design/dao.star.md; rg -n 'Complete history|complete-history|attachment|serial|concurr|portable-values' docs/design/dao.stream.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '46,255p' src/cljc/dao/star/lease.cljc; sed -n '78,103p' docs/design/dao.star.md; rg -n 'Complete history|complete-history|attachment|serial|concurr|portable-values' docs/design/dao.stream.md\"","aggregated_output":"(defn make-agent\n  \"A holder over `lease/make-holder` plus the cursors its control flow drains.\n   `config` is `make-holder`'s, less the cursors (minted here at the oldest\n   anchor, so a grant already on the medium is observed).  `:envelope` is merged\n   into every fact the agent appends (the lineage lease stamps\n   `:dao.star/lineage` here, which is what the judge's resolver attributes by).\n   Answers an atom holding the agent state.\"\n  [{:keys [tick fact writer envelope] :as config}]\n  (let [wired (lease/make-holder\n                (assoc config\n                       :tick {:handle tick :cursor (oldest-cursor tick)}\n                       :fact {:handle (:handle fact)\n                              :cursor (oldest-cursor (:handle fact))\n                              :source (:source fact)\n                              :medium (:medium fact)}\n                       :writer writer))]\n    (atom {:holder (:holder wired)\n           :tick (:tick wired)\n           :fact (:fact wired)\n           :writer (:writer wired)\n           :envelope (or envelope {})\n           :reading nil\n           :lapsed? false\n           :gapped? false\n           :release nil})))\n\n\n(defn- lease-id\n  [a]\n  (get-in a [:holder :grant :dao.lease/lease]))\n\n\n(defn step!\n  \"One control-flow pass of the holder: drain its own tick cursor for the\n   newest reading, drain the fact cursor observing its grant (before anything\n   else) and any `:lapsed` record for its lease.  A `gap` on either cursor\n   marks the agent `:gapped?`: it renews nothing from then on.  Answers the\n   new state.\"\n  [agent]\n  (swap!\n    agent\n    (fn [a]\n      (let [t (drain (get-in a [:tick :handle]) (get-in a [:tick :cursor]))\n            reading (or (some-> (filter #(= :dao.lease/tick (:dao.lease/event %))\n                                        (:values t))\n                                last\n                                :dao.lease/reading)\n                        (:reading a))\n            f (drain (get-in a [:fact :handle]) (get-in a [:fact :cursor]))\n            a (-> a\n                  (assoc :reading reading)\n                  (assoc-in [:tick :cursor] (:cursor t))\n                  (assoc-in [:fact :cursor] (:cursor f))\n                  (update :gapped? #(or % (:gap? f))))]\n        (reduce\n          (fn [a v]\n            (cond\n              (and (nil? (get-in a [:holder :grant])) reading)\n              (update a :holder lease/observe-grant (get-in a [:fact :source]) v reading)\n\n              (and (= :dao.lease/lapsed (:dao.lease/status v))\n                   (some? (lease-id a))\n                   (= (lease-id a) (:dao.lease/lease v)))\n              (assoc a :lapsed? true)\n\n              :else a))\n          a\n          (:values f))))))\n\n\n(defn holding?\n  \"May the control flow act: a grant observed, not stopped, not at its bound,\n   not lapsed, and no gap seen.\"\n  [agent]\n  (let [a @agent]\n    (boolean (and (not (:lapsed? a))\n                  (not (:gapped? a))\n                  (some? (:reading a))\n                  (lease/holding? (:holder a) (:reading a))))))\n\n\n(defn granted?\n  [agent]\n  (some? (get-in @agent [:holder :grant])))\n\n\n(defn past-bound?\n  \"True once the agent has left the lease for good: it lapsed, was released,\n   or reached its bound.  A gap is not that: the agent renews nothing after one\n   but the lease is not known to be over.\"\n  [agent]\n  (let [a @agent]\n    (boolean (or (:lapsed? a)\n                 (get-in a [:holder :released?])\n                 (get-in a [:holder :bound-reached?])\n                 (and (some? (:reading a)) (some? (get-in a [:holder :grant]))\n                      (lease/at-bound? (:holder a) (:reading a)))))))\n\n\n(defn- append-renewal!\n  [agent]\n  (let [a @agent\n        fact (merge (lease/renewal (lease-id a)) (:envelope a))\n        outcome (stream/append! (get-in a [:writer :handle]) fact)]\n    (swap! agent update :holder lease/observe-renewal (:reading a) outcome)\n    outcome))\n\n\n(defn renew-if-due!\n  \"Renew when the holder's interval has been reached.  Answers true when a\n   renewal was appended.\"\n  [agent]\n  (let [a @agent]\n    (boolean\n      (when (and (holding? agent) (lease/due-to-renew? (:holder a) (:reading a)))\n        (append-renewal! agent)\n        true))))\n\n\n(defn renew!\n  \"Renew now, on a consumed input.  A holder that is not holding renews\n   nothing.\"\n  [agent]\n  (boolean (when (holding? agent) (append-renewal! agent) true)))\n\n\n(defn release!\n  \"Release on halt.  The release fact is kept until its append answers ok, so a\n   failed append retries the same fact.\"\n  [agent]\n  (let [a @agent]\n    (when (and (granted? agent) (not (get-in a [:holder :released?])))\n      (let [{:keys [holder release]} (lease/stop (:holder a))]\n        (swap! agent assoc :holder holder :release (merge release (:envelope a)))))\n    (when-let [fact (:release @agent)]\n      (when (ok? (stream/append! (get-in @agent [:writer :handle]) fact))\n        (swap! agent assoc :release nil :released-sent? true)))\n    agent))\n\n\n;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; Grantor side: exchange lease\n;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(def resolver-bindings #{:per-author-media :envelope-key})\n\n(def exchange-source :egress)\n(def lineage-source :session-facts)\n(def exchange-lease-source :exchange-lease)\n(def lineage-lease-source :lineage-lease)\n(def exchange-grantor :boundary-judge)\n(def lineage-grantor :lineage-judge)\n\n\n(defn resolver\n  \"The one attribution the star compositions share.  Per-author media: the\n   source names the author.  Envelope key: the session-facts medium is written\n   only by session drivers, each stamping `:dao.star/lineage`, and that stamp\n   names the author.  A fact's own claim of authorship is never consulted.\"\n  [source fact]\n  (if (= lineage-source source)\n    (when-let [s (:dao.star/lineage fact)] {:dao.star/lineage s})\n    (case source\n      :egress :egress\n      :exchange-lease exchange-grantor\n      :lineage-lease lineage-grantor\n      nil)))\n\n\n(defn medium-declaration\n  [capacity attribution]\n  {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity capacity\n   :value-domain :portable-values :attribution attribution})\n\n\n(defn make-exchange-lease\n  \"The grantor half of the exchange lease, composed inside the peer holding the\n   HTTP boundary.  Config:\n     :ingress :egress :lease-medium  the three media (handles)\n     :tick                           the judge's tick stream (handle)\n     :open-exchanges :close-exchange the boundary's inventory and reclaim\n     :units :duration :cadence :tolerance\n     :capacity                       declared capacity of the egress medium\n   The judge reads the egress medium for the responders' renewals and writes\n   grants and `:lapsed` to the lease medium.  Policy ends the lease of an\n   exchange the inventory no longer holds (peer close, gap reconciliation), and\n   reclaim is the boundary's idempotent `close-exchange`, reporting success when\n   the exchange is not open afterwards.\"\n  [{:keys [ingress egress lease-medium tick open-exchanges close-exchange\n           units duration cadence tolerance capacity]}]\n  (let [reclaim (fn [subject]\n                  (let [id (:http/exchange subject)]\n                    (close-exchange id)\n                    (not (contains? (open-exchanges) id))))\n        policy (fn [entry _now]\n                 (not (contains? (open-exchanges)\n                                 (:http/exchange (:subject entry)))))\n        made (lease/make-judge\n               {:units units :cadence cadence :tolerance tolerance\n                :resolver resolver :resolver-bindings resolver-bindings\n                :reclaim reclaim :policy policy\n                :writer lease-medium :self exchange-grantor\n                :ticks [{:handle tick :cursor (oldest-cursor tick)}]\n                :media [{:handle egress :cursor (oldest-cursor egress)\n                         :source exchange-source\n                         :medium (medium-declaration capacity :per-author-media)}]})]\n    (atom {:judge (:judge made) :step (:step made)\n           :ingress ingress :ingress-cursor (oldest-cursor ingress)\n           :open-exchanges open-exchanges\n           :duration duration :leased #{}})))\n**The token is the gate.** It is the request's only routing and idempotence key, and until ShiBi is load-bearing it is the sole gate on Mode 1 input: a pre-shared value in `dao.shibi.md`'s sense (owner ruling 2026-10-07).\n\n**Order is the ingress position.** Two inputs for one occurrence are not concurrent once deposited: one is earlier. Custody decides who consumes it. In a one-process composition the session's single driver is the only resumer; that exclusion is process-scoped and says so. Where more than one peer observes the ingress, resumption is a take, and a take is a lease on the occurrence (UCF §7.7).\n\n**One input, one successor.** Consuming an input advances occurrence `O` to its successor `O'` and appends the lineage fact. The reply goes to the exchange that carried the consumed input; patches for the session go to its open subscription exchanges, which the driver holds as its own interpreter state, built from the subscribe requests and terminal events routed to it.\n\n**Stale input is one-shot** (owner ruling 2026-10-07). A double click, a retry, a replayed URL, a second tab or the back button names an `O` that already has a successor. It runs nothing and is re-projected. The UI is a derivation, so answering twice is harmless, and a retry whose first reply was lost still converges. Mode 1 continuations are one-shot; multi-shot forks are deferred.\n\n**Effects.** Exactly-once needs a fenced writer into an enrolled consumer (UCF §7.7.5). Every other stream is at-least-once and declared so.\n\n### Liveness\n\nTwo leased resources, kept apart. Neither adds a clock to the wait for input: a parked continuation's `next` on its input is `blocked` until a request arrives, on a Tuesday or a Thursday.\n\n**The open exchange is leased.** The judge runs inside the peer that holds the HTTP boundary and is composed with the boundary's `close-exchange` as reclaim procedure and `open-exchanges` as its inventory (`dao.stream.http.md`, Inventory). For each `:http/request` it observes it grants unsolicited on a lease medium it writes: subject `{:http/exchange x}`, holder the egress medium's identity, a duration in `{:ms 1 :s 1000}`. Reclaim closes the exchange; the adapter deposits `:http/closed`, then the judge records `:lapsed`. A responder that keeps an exchange open observes its grant and appends `{:dao.lease/event :dao.lease/renewal :dao.lease/lease L}` to the egress medium at under half the duration, from its own control flow, against its own tick stream. The judge and `egress-step` are peer observers of that medium; each ignores the other's facts. A one-shot responder answers inside the granted duration and renews nothing. An exchange nobody answers lapses by `:silence`; Datastar's reconnect opens a new one.\n\n**A gap is loss, and nothing is forwarded about it.** The judge, on an ingress `gap`, reconciles both ways against the inventory: an open exchange without a lease is granted afresh, and a leased exchange absent from the inventory is recorded `:lapsed` with cause `:policy`, so nothing is held unleased and nothing closed stays leased (inventory reconciliation; `dao.lease.md`'s reclaim-and-regrant is reserved for a lost ledger). The router forwards nothing about a gap: a request or terminal event lost in the evicted window is unrouted, and a forward whose `append!` answers anything but `ok` is the same loss; an unrouted request's exchange lapses by `:silence`. Drivers learn that an exchange is gone from the lease medium they already read for their grants: a `:lapsed` record for one of their exchanges drops it (`dao.lease.md`, Carriage). A driver whose cursor on any medium it reads answers `gap` forgets every subscription it holds and renews none; they lapse by `:silence` and close, and Datastar's reconnect subscribes again. Session media are declared at assembly like any deposit destination, evict-oldest with a capacity, and sized against the driver's lag.\n\n**Keep-alive is the responder's.** On its tick it may append an `:http/chunk` carrying an SSE comment line. That chunk is bytes for the wire, so the host discovers a dead peer by writing; the renewal is evidence for the judge. Neither stands in for the other. A host whose send buffers (http-kit) may not report a peer that disconnects while an exchange is idle; the exchange lapses by `:silence` and is closed by reclaim, with latency bounded by the lease duration plus judge cadence. A peer's close or a failed write is deposited as `:http/closed`; the responder reads it as data and drops the exchange, and the judge ends the exchange lease with cause `:policy`.\n\n**The lineage is leased** (owner ruling 2026-10-07; the holder choice below is the architect's). A lineage nobody returns to is reclaimed through `dao.lease.md`, not by a timer. The peer holding the parked record is the grantor. When a lineage begins, its judge grants unsolicited on the lease medium: subject and holder `{:dao.star/lineage S}`, duration the composition's idle allowance, `:dao.lease/max` optional. Attribution is by envelope key: the session-facts medium is written only by session drivers, each stamping `:dao.star/lineage` on its facts, renewals and release, and the judge's resolver reads that key; until ShiBi, any writer of that medium can renew, the same exposure the exchange lease has. The driver observes its grant before consuming or projecting, renews at under half the duration from its own control flow, on each consumed input and on its tick while it holds an open subscription, and **stops at its bound**: past it, it consumes nothing and projects nothing, and an input arriving then is handed to the root program as begin. So a connected session is retained for as long as it stays connected, by design, bounded only by the cap; a disconnected one lapses after the idle allowance. The lease ends with the lineage: released by the driver on halt, lapsed by the judge on silence. Reclaim retires the runnable resource, the current parked record; the `:lapsed` record on the lease medium is the judge's own and is what ends the lineage for the router. History, successor facts and lease records are kept (`dao.lease.md`: a reclaim frees the resource, never the record). The subject is distinct from Mode 2's custody subject `{:yin.k/occurrence O}` on the arbitration medium. Leases are process-scoped until the composition settles the three durable duties `dao.lease.md` names.\n\nSizing: duration exceeds twice the renewal interval; the keep-alive interval stays under the shortest proxy or NAT idle timeout on the path; the ingress window exceeds router and judge lag and each session medium's window exceeds its driver's; a boundary restart loses sockets and ledger together, so its exchange inventory to reclaim is empty. On hosts whose sends buffer, the exchange lease's duration is also the dead-peer detection bound. A false lapse is possible (`dao.lease.md`, Limits).\n\n---\n\n48:Creation is not attachment. A descriptor is not a creation specification or an\n90:  handle on it, stable across attachment lifecycles and across serialization.\n231:  Both projections are total and outlive any attachment, so `descriptor` has\n234:  attachment to the **same** logical stream the descriptor names. Attaching\n240:Streams are values that can be sent through streams — up to a serialization\n250:is a serialization boundary. Descriptors exist for crossing those\n294:- A transport whose attachments are distinguishable assigns each attachment\n295:  an opaque, structurally serializable value, unique among the attachments\n296:  that transport can tell apart. Every attachment handle the transport mints\n299:  `attach!` success map carries the value under `:dao.stream/attachment`.\n303:  attachment is displaced onto another channel, the same value correlates it\n306:  transport's. Transports that cannot distinguish attachments omit it.\n309:  Whether attachment should be gated at all, and by what, is a question this\n327:the host serialization codec structurally unchanged, so equality is\n345:| `:dao.stream/ok`                 | A handle exists through which this attachment is operated. Implies neither that a far end has confirmed the stream it names nor that establishment has completed. Where either answer is one only the far end can give, it arrives later as data, on the channel the transport names (see Surfaces). | `:dao.stream/handle`, and `:dao.stream/attachment` where the transport distinguishes attachments |\n365:Creation defers differently from attachment, and the difference is why this is\n417:reachability and logical-stream identity, because both outlive any attachment.\n514:  `:dao.stream/invalid-anchor`. On a handle whose attachment has closed,\n554:  survives the host serialization codec structurally unchanged, under the\n643:server-side accepted-connection handle is an attachment and does not gain\n645:handle is on an attachment: closing it ends that attachment only — the\n652:and `cursor-mismatch` is logical-stream-relative.) After an attachment\n654:`ok` with reachability and identity — both outlive any attachment; a reader surface, where the\n657:minted through a closed attachment. Cursors bind to the logical stream,\n660:Closing an attachment freezes what that handle can still observe: values\n662:`end` is reached at the position the stream had reached when the attachment\n686:further about concurrent operations.\n730:### Complete history\n764:The obligation a complete-history transport takes on is one sentence: **a\n765:complete-history reader begins at its logical sequence's origin and never\n773:What it owes on the writing side depends on what it is. A complete-history\n861:**The assumption.** *Complete history* obliges a transport to retain every\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
