{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'co-locat|session-facts|read first|Scope|criterion|memory-log' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792832568086-architect-dao-star-m1-phase-b-scope.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md; nl -ba test/dao/star/driver_test.clj | sed -n '138,155p;305,332p;402,435p;474,520p'; nl -ba test/dao/star/loopback_test.clj | sed -n '136,182p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/http/jvm.clj | sed -n '24,65p'; rg -n 'tick|reading' test/dao/lease_test.cljc | tail -10\"","aggregated_output":"58:- This reading should be stated in the Phase B brief and in the criterion's test. The driver is the only part that does I/O, and the program is pure sequential logic over `<!` and `>!`.\n61:- (b), a bespoke step function over parked state. It would not exercise the CESK parking surface at all, and the criterion names a `yin.vm` agent.\n86:2. Drain the session-facts cursor to `blocked`, folding each fact into the index via `facts/index-step`.\n97:**Co-location constraint:** an assembly-time assertion in the router constructor. The facts and lease handles must be direct, non-reflection handles, tested with `(not (satisfies? ... reflection))` or an explicit `:co-located? true` declaration at assembly. It throws ex-info with `:refused`, as the lease constructors do.\n124:- **Judge:** `lease/make-judge` over the session-facts and lease media. `:resolver-bindings` must cover envelope-key attribution (`:dao.star/lineage`). The reclaim procedure drops the parked record: the `await` result and the session's media handles.\n200:8. **Scope creep into Mode 2.** The brief should state that no UCF, custody or export code is in Phase B.\n   138\t            :begin begin :ticks ticks :open open :clock clock :driver drv\n   139\t            :xl xl :ll ll :router rt :next-exchange (atom 0)\n   140\t            :egress-cursor (atom (lease/oldest-cursor egress))\n   141\t            :interval interval}]\n   142\t     (assoc w :close-exchange close-exchange))))\n   143\t\n   144\t\n   145\t(defn boundary-step!\n   146\t  \"The fake boundary's egress interpretation: an `:http/end` for an open\n   147\t   exchange completes it and deposits `:http/ended`.\"\n   148\t  [{:keys [egress egress-cursor open ingress]}]\n   149\t  (let [r (lease/drain egress @egress-cursor)]\n   150\t    (reset! egress-cursor (:cursor r))\n   151\t    (doseq [v (:values r)\n   152\t            :when (and (= :http/end (:http/effect v)) (contains? @open (:http/exchange v)))]\n   153\t      (swap! open disj (:http/exchange v))\n   154\t      (stream/append! ingress {:http/exchange (:http/exchange v) :http/event :http/ended}))))\n   155\t\n   305\t;; Clause: stale token is re-projected\n   306\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   307\t\n   308\t(deftest stale-token-is-reprojected-and_runs-nothing\n   309\t  (let [w (start! (world))\n   310\t        s (begin-lineage! w)\n   311\t        o1 (occ-of (sse-text w (input! w s \"{\\\"inc\\\":4}\")))\n   312\t        facts-before (count (consumption-facts w))\n   313\t        stale (input! w s \"{\\\"inc\\\":4}\")]\n   314\t    (is (= facts-before (count (consumption-facts w))))\n   315\t    (is (= [:http/head :http/chunk :http/end] (mapv :http/effect (effects w stale))))\n   316\t    (is (= o1 (occ-of (sse-text w stale))) \"the projection of the current occurrence\")\n   317\t    (is (str/includes? (sse-text w stale) \">4<\") \"the continuation did not run again\")))\n   318\t\n   319\t\n   320\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   321\t;; Fact before UI\n   322\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   323\t\n   324\t(deftest no-ui-with-the-successor-id-before-its-fact-is-accepted\n   325\t  (let [w (start! (world))\n   326\t        s (begin-lineage! w)\n   327\t        _ (reset! (:failing? w) true)\n   328\t        x (input! w s \"{\\\"inc\\\":1}\")]\n   329\t    (testing \"the fact append answered non-ok: nothing is projected\"\n   330\t      (is (empty? (effects w x)))\n   331\t      (is (empty? (consumption-facts w)))\n   332\t      (is (= {:occurrence s :model {:count 0}} (driver/latest (:driver w) s))))\n   402\t;; A just-published token is never answered as begin\n   403\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   404\t\n   405\t(defn- chase!\n   406\t  \"Post immediately to the token each answer publishes, `n` times.\"\n   407\t  [w n]\n   408\t  (let [s (begin-lineage! w)]\n   409\t    (loop [token s i 1]\n   410\t      (if (> i n)\n   411\t        token\n   412\t        (let [x (input! w token \"{\\\"inc\\\":1}\")\n   413\t              text (sse-text w x)]\n   414\t          (is (str/includes? text (str \">\" i \"<\")) (str \"input \" i \" was consumed, not begun\"))\n   415\t          (recur (occ-of text) (inc i)))))))\n   416\t\n   417\t\n   418\t(deftest just-published-token-is-never-begin\n   419\t  (let [w (start! (world))]\n   420\t    (chase! w 25)\n   421\t    (is (= 25 (count (consumption-facts w))))\n   422\t    (is (= 1 (count (driver/sessions (:driver w)))))))\n   423\t\n   424\t\n   425\t(deftest ^:slow just-published-token-is-never-begin-stress\n   426\t  (let [w (start! (world {:duration-ms 1000000 :facts-capacity 2048 :session-capacity 1024}))]\n   427\t    (chase! w 400)\n   428\t    (is (= 400 (count (consumption-facts w))))\n   429\t    (is (= 1 (count (driver/sessions (:driver w)))))))\n   430\t\n   431\t\n   432\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   433\t;; Ingress gap: reconciliation both ways\n   434\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   435\t\n   474\t  (let [[w _ _] (subscribed-world {})]\n   475\t    (dotimes [_ 6] (advance! w 10))\n   476\t    (is (pos? (renewals w)))))\n   477\t\n   478\t\n   479\t(deftest driver-stops-renewing-after-observing-the-lapse\n   480\t  (let [[w s sub] (subscribed-world {:duration-ms 1000})\n   481\t        lease-id (some #(when (= {:http/exchange sub} (:dao.lease/subject %))\n   482\t                          (:dao.lease/lease %))\n   483\t                       (values (:exchange-lease w)))]\n   484\t    (dotimes [_ 30] (advance! w 10))\n   485\t    (is (pos? (renewals w)) \"renewing while the lease is live\")\n   486\t    (stream/append! (:exchange-lease w) (dl/lapsed lease-id :policy))\n   487\t    (pump! w)\n   488\t    (is (not (contains? (driver/subscriptions (:driver w) s) sub)) \"the exchange is dropped\")\n   489\t    (let [before (renewals w)]\n   490\t      (dotimes [_ 10] (advance! w 10))\n   491\t      (is (= before (renewals w)) \"no renewal appended after the lapse\"))))\n   492\t\n   493\t\n   494\t(deftest driver-stops-renewing-after-its-own-gap\n   495\t  (let [[w s _] (subscribed-world {:duration-ms 1000 :session-capacity 2})]\n   496\t    (dotimes [_ 30] (advance! w 10))\n   497\t    (is (pos? (renewals w)))\n   498\t    (dotimes [_ 6]\n   499\t      (stream/append! (driver/session-medium (:driver w) s)\n   500\t                      {:exchange [9 9] :kind :terminal}))\n   501\t    (driver/driver-step! (:driver w))\n   502\t    (is (empty? (driver/subscriptions (:driver w) s)) \"subscriptions forgotten\")\n   503\t    (let [before (renewals w)]\n   504\t      (dotimes [_ 10] (advance! w 10))\n   505\t      (is (= before (renewals w)) \"no renewal appended after the gap\"))))\n   506\t\n   507\t\n   508\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   509\t;; Renewal in flight counts while live; one after retirement does not revive\n   510\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   511\t\n   512\t(deftest renewal-in-flight-counts-while-live-and-does-not-revive-a-retired-lease\n   513\t  (let [w (start! (world))\n   514\t        x (call! w :get \"/unrouted\")\n   515\t        _ (pump! w)\n   516\t        lease-id (some #(when (= {:http/exchange x} (:dao.lease/subject %))\n   517\t                          (:dao.lease/lease %))\n   518\t                       (values (:exchange-lease w)))\n   519\t        ledger #(get-in @(:xl w) [:judge :ledger])\n   520\t        lapsed #(count (filter (fn [f] (= :dao.lease/lapsed (:dao.lease/status f)))\n   136\t(deftest a-closed-socket-is-observed-as-http-closed\n   137\t  ;; http-kit never reports a client-initiated close of an idle streaming\n   138\t  ;; exchange (reproduced without any dao code: no on-close after FIN or RST\n   139\t  ;; and further writes), so the socket here is closed from the boundary's side\n   140\t  ;; by the reclaim procedure, and the test asserts what the composition then\n   141\t  ;; observes: the client sees EOF, the ingress carries :http/closed for that\n   142\t  ;; exchange, and the driver reads it as data and drops the exchange.\n   143\t  (let [{:keys [port ingress boundary drv stop!]} (compose)]\n   144\t    (try\n   145\t      (let [page (roundtrip port \"GET\" \"/\" nil)\n   146\t            s (second (re-find #\"data-root=\\\"([^\\\"]+)\\\"\" page))]\n   147\t        (with-open [sock (doto (Socket. \"127.0.0.1\" (int port)) (.setSoTimeout 5000))]\n   148\t          (send-request sock \"GET\" (str \"/s/\" s) nil true)\n   149\t          (let [in (.getInputStream sock)\n   150\t                buf (byte-array 4096)\n   151\t                seen (StringBuilder.)]\n   152\t            (is (wait-for 5000\n   153\t                          #(do (when (pos? (.available in))\n   154\t                                 (let [n (.read in buf)]\n   155\t                                   (.append seen (String. buf 0 n \"UTF-8\"))))\n   156\t                               (str/includes? (str seen) \"data-occ\"))))\n   157\t            (let [id (:http/exchange\n   158\t                       (wait-for 3000\n   159\t                                 #(first (filter (fn [e] (and (= :http/request (:http/event e))\n   160\t                                                              (= (str \"/s/\" s) (:http/path e))))\n   161\t                                                 (h/values ingress)))))]\n   162\t              (is (some? id))\n   163\t              (is (contains? (driver/subscriptions drv s) id))\n   164\t              (is (true? (http/close-exchange boundary id)))\n   165\t              (is (wait-for 3000\n   166\t                            #(some (fn [e] (and (= id (:http/exchange e))\n   167\t                                                (= :http/closed (:http/event e))))\n   168\t                                   (h/values ingress)))\n   169\t                  \"the closed socket is deposited as :http/closed\")\n   170\t              (is (not (contains? (http/open-exchanges boundary) id)))\n   171\t              (is (wait-for 3000\n   172\t                            #(do (when (pos? (.available in))\n   173\t                                   (let [n (.read in buf)]\n   174\t                                     (.append seen (String. buf 0 n \"UTF-8\"))))\n   175\t                                 (str/ends-with? (str seen) \"0\\r\\n\\r\\n\")))\n   176\t                  \"the client reads the response to its end\")\n   177\t              (is (wait-for 3000 #(not (contains? (driver/subscriptions drv s) id)))\n   178\t                  \"the driver drops the exchange\")))))\n   179\t      (finally (stop!)))))\n   180\t\n   181\t\n   182\t(deftest agent-receives-answers-and-resumes-over-the-real-boundary\nnl: src/cljc/dao/stream/http/jvm.clj: No such file or directory\n2498:  (testing \"D3/4.4#4: the reference driver appends non-decreasing readings\"\n2500:          driver (tick-driver buffer)]\n2503:            readings (mapv #(get % :dao.lease/reading) values)]\n2504:        (is (= 5 (count readings)) \"five deposits appended five ticks\")\n2506:            \"each deposit is a well-formed tick fact\")\n2509:                    (map vector readings (rest readings)))\n2510:            \"readings never decrease across deposits\")))))\n2513:(deftest tick-driver-stops-on-demand-test\n2516:          driver (tick-driver buffer)]\n2522:      (is (= 1 ((:appended driver))) \"exactly the one pre-stop tick landed\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
